IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 248 of 2020
CITATION: (2020) 7 SCC 1
YEAR: 2020

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: R.F. Nariman, S. Ravindra Bhat, V. Ramasubramanian

PARTIES:
Arjun Panditrao Khotkar vs Kailash Kushanrao Gorantyal

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Indian Evidence Act, 1872, Information Technology Act, 2000

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 65B Evidence Act, Section 65A Evidence Act

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
electronic records, certificate mandatory, secondary evidence, digital proof, call records

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Settled conflicting precedents by ruling that a certificate under Section 65B(4) is an absolute condition precedent for the admissibility of electronic records as secondary evidence in legal proceedings.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 65B Evidence Act, Section 65A Evidence Act.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

